(WHITECOLLAR / CONSULTATION PREPARATION GUIDE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A practical checklist for an introductory conversation.) Tj T*
(Demonstration resource - not a contract or a service proposal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Describe the problem) Tj T*
(Write down one decision or operational challenge you want to discuss.) Tj T*
(Include an example of what happens today and who it affects.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Define the outcome) Tj T*
(Describe what a useful result would look like for your team.) Tj T*
(Note any deadlines, dependencies or constraints.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Gather existing information) Tj T*
(Bring the process notes, plans or reports you already use.) Tj T*
(Identify missing information without sharing confidential data.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Identify the people involved) Tj T*
(List who owns the process and who can approve the next step.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Prepare your questions) Tj T*
(Ask about scope, deliverables, timing and responsibilities.) Tj T*
(Agree on a written summary and a date for the next conversation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Use this guide as a discussion aid. No results are guaranteed.) Tj T*
